2026-10-08T07:19:38.5148663Z [1;31mSwitching to the Multi-user Installer[0m
2026-10-08T07:19:38.5248485Z [32mWelcome to the Multi-User Nix Installation
2026-10-08T07:19:38.5258734Z [0m
2026-10-08T07:19:38.5259453Z This installation tool will set up your computer with the Nix package
2026-10-08T07:19:38.5260476Z manager. This will happen in a few stages:
2026-10-08T07:19:38.5261009Z 
2026-10-08T07:19:38.5262050Z 1. Make sure your computer doesn't already have Nix. If it does, I
2026-10-08T07:19:38.5263081Z    will show you instructions on how to clean up your old install.
2026-10-08T07:19:38.5263582Z 
2026-10-08T07:19:38.5265111Z 2. Show you what I am going to install and where. Then I will ask
2026-10-08T07:19:38.5265865Z    if you are ready to continue.
2026-10-08T07:19:38.5266437Z 
2026-10-08T07:19:38.5267603Z 3. Create the system users [34m(uids [30001..30008])[0m and groups [34m(gid 30000)[0m
2026-10-08T07:19:38.5268498Z    that the Nix daemon uses to run builds. To create system users
2026-10-08T07:19:38.5269118Z    in a different range, exit and run this tool again with
2026-10-08T07:19:38.5269604Z    NIX_FIRST_BUILD_UID set.
2026-10-08T07:19:38.5269907Z 
2026-10-08T07:19:38.5270270Z 4. Perform the basic installation of the Nix files daemon.
2026-10-08T07:19:38.5270671Z 
2026-10-08T07:19:38.5271080Z 5. Configure your shell to import special Nix Profile files, so you
2026-10-08T07:19:38.5271598Z    can use Nix.
2026-10-08T07:19:38.5271866Z 
2026-10-08T07:19:38.5272129Z 6. Start the Nix daemon.
2026-10-08T07:19:38.5272659Z 
2026-10-08T07:19:38.5273212Z [32m[4;32mWould you like to see a more detailed list of what I will do?
2026-10-08T07:19:38.5273856Z [0mNo TTY, assuming you would say yes :)
2026-10-08T07:19:38.5274654Z 
2026-10-08T07:19:38.5274894Z I will:
2026-10-08T07:19:38.5275153Z 
2026-10-08T07:19:38.5275492Z  - make sure your computer doesn't already have Nix files
2026-10-08T07:19:38.5276059Z    (if it does, I will tell you how to clean them up.)
2026-10-08T07:19:38.5276635Z  - create local users (see the list above for the users I'll make)
2026-10-08T07:19:38.5277170Z  - create a local group (nixbld)
2026-10-08T07:19:38.5277586Z  - install Nix in /nix
2026-10-08T07:19:38.5277999Z  - create a configuration file in /etc/nix
2026-10-08T07:19:38.5278872Z  - set up the "default profile" by creating some Nix-related files in
2026-10-08T07:19:38.5279816Z    /root
2026-10-08T07:19:38.5287283Z  - back up /etc/bash.bashrc to /etc/bash.bashrc.backup-before-nix
2026-10-08T07:19:38.5288019Z  - update /etc/bash.bashrc to include some Nix configuration
2026-10-08T07:19:38.5300898Z  - load and start a service (at /etc/systemd/system/nix-daemon.service
2026-10-08T07:19:38.5301609Z    and /etc/systemd/system/nix-daemon.socket) for nix-daemon
2026-10-08T07:19:38.5301935Z 
2026-10-08T07:19:38.5302468Z [32m[4;32mReady to continue?
2026-10-08T07:19:38.5302885Z [0mNo TTY, assuming you would say yes :)
2026-10-08T07:19:38.5320988Z 
2026-10-08T07:19:38.5322047Z [34m---- let's talk about sudo -----------------------------------------------------
2026-10-08T07:19:38.5331861Z [0mThis script is going to call sudo a lot. Normally, it would show you
2026-10-08T07:19:38.5332906Z exactly what commands it is running and why. However, the script is
2026-10-08T07:19:38.5333697Z run in a headless fashion, like this:
2026-10-08T07:19:38.5335048Z 
2026-10-08T07:19:38.5335366Z   $ curl -L https://nixos.org/nix/install | sh
2026-10-08T07:19:38.5335785Z 
2026-10-08T07:19:38.5336264Z or maybe in a CI pipeline. Because of that, I'm going to skip the
2026-10-08T07:19:38.5337046Z verbose output in the interest of brevity.
2026-10-08T07:19:38.5337414Z 
2026-10-08T07:19:38.5337596Z If you would like to
2026-10-08T07:19:38.5338025Z see the output, try like this:
2026-10-08T07:19:38.5338207Z 
2026-10-08T07:19:38.5338433Z   $ curl -L -o install-nix https://nixos.org/nix/install
2026-10-08T07:19:38.5338792Z   $ sh ./install-nix
